    "updated_at": "2023-01-09T15:30:01Z",
    "body": "Okay, thanks! That solves a part of the problem.\r\n\r\nSince I took the code verbatim from the docs, you might want to update the example for transient so that others don't make the same mistake I did.\r\n\r\nI still have some funky behavior though. I run `fish` I get no transient prompt, but if I run `fish -N -C \"source ~/.config/fish/config.fish\"` I do. As I don't have anything in `.config/fish/conf.d/` I imagine that something happens outside the scope of my configuration.\r\n\r\nI willing to do some diagnostics on my own, but I need help. what files does `fish` source? `/etc/fish/` contains empty files. Losts is going on in `/usr/share/fish`, but sourcing it `fish -N -C /usr/share/fish/config.fish` does not replicate the issue I'm experiencing. Any pointers would be helpful.",
